# TypeScript standards

- Keep TypeScript strict and derive API types from versioned contracts.
- Put product behavior under one feature directory; shared UI must be domain-neutral.
- Server state uses query clients; transient canvas state stays local to the feature.
- Never trust localStorage as account identity or product truth.
- Handle loading, error, offline, keyboard, responsive, and reduced-motion states.
- Add component tests and an end-to-end scenario for every user-visible workflow.

